LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Open Studio: First Thursdays
DESCRIPTION:Our Open Studio program invites participants to be creative i
 n the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for reflection\, exp
 ression\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist\, the open st
 udio welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their own pace while d
 rawing inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art experience is
  needed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, and we'll ha
 ndle the rest!  Participants are welcome to utilize supplies located in t
 he studio\, as well as bring their own supplies/projects to work on.  Thi
 s program occurs during First Thursday each month. It is open to everyone
 : students\, staff\, and the public included! The group will meet in the 
 Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Ed
 ucation on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Our Open Studio program invites partici
 pants to be creative in the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a too
 l for reflection\, expression\, and connection. Guided by a trained art t
 herapist\, the open studio welcomes visitors to engage with materials at 
 their own pace while drawing inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions
 . No art experience is needed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to
  create\, and we'll handle the rest!</p><p>  Participants are welcome to 
 utilize supplies located in the studio\, as well as bring their own suppl
 ies/projects to work on.</p><p>  This program occurs during First Thursda
 y each month. It is open to everyone: students\, staff\, and the public i
 ncluded! The group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, loca
 ted inside the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Esken
 azi Museum of Art.</p>
