SUMMARY:Brandon Gunn: McKinney Visiting Artist Series lecture
DESCRIPTION:Since 2016\, Gunn has been Education Director at the Tamarind
  Institute\, a globally recognized center for fine art lithography in Alb
 uquerque\, New Mexico. He is also the owner of arcEditions\, a premier U.
 S. maker of leather rollers.Gunn has taught printmaking at IU Bloomington
 \, Concordia University (Montreal)\, and Brigham Young University (BYU)-I
 daho and has consulted with institutions including the Roswell Artist-in-
 Residence Program (N.M.)\, Santa Reparata (Florence\, Italy)\, and BYU to
  design studios\, streamline workflows\, and integrate lithography into t
 heir programs. He has also collaborated with manufacturers such as Takach
  Press (Albuquerque) and Cranfield Colours (Wales\, UK) to develop and en
 sure reliable\, high-quality materials for the field.  &#160\;The McKinne
 y Visiting Artist Series brings prominent working artists from a range of
  studio practices and fields to the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture
  + Design. Artists lead workshops and critiques for students within the d
 epartment\, as well as lectures and gallery talks open to the campus comm
 unity.The College of Arts and Sciences and the Eskenazi School of Art\, A
 rchitecture + Design gratefully acknowledge Dr. Meredith McKinney (B.A. '
 65) and Elsa Luise Barthel McKinney (B.A. '65) for their love of the arts
  and their generous support in endowing the McKinney Visiting Artist Seri
 es at Indiana University Bloomington.
