SUMMARY:Opening Reception\, Samuel Levi Jones: An Archaeology of Knowledge
DESCRIPTION:5:00–7:00 p.m. | Opening reception\,hors d'oeuvres and cash
  bar\, 2nd floor atriumAbout the Artist:  Known for his large-scale abstr
 act assemblages made from deconstructed encyclopedias\, law books\, medic
 al texts\, and other printed materials\, Jones transforms sources of inst
 itutional knowledge into richly textured works that question how informat
 ion\,history\,andauthorityareconstructed.Bydismantlingandreconstructingth
 esematerials\,hisworkexaminessystemsthatshapeculturalnarratives\,power\,a
 ndprivilegeintheUnitedStates.DrawinginspirationfromtheideasofFrenchphilos
 opherMichelFoucault\,SamuelLeviJones:AnArchaeologyofKnowledge brings toge
 ther works spanning ten years of Jones's practice. For this presentation\
 , Jones also engaged with the Eskenazi Museum of Art's collection\,identi
 fyingworksthatresonatewiththemescentraltohisresearch\,includingnationalis
 mandpatriotism\,censorship\,andtherepresentationofmarginalizedidentitiesi
 nhistoricalnarratives.  For more information including museum location\, 
 where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.
