SUMMARY:New Acquisitions Open House
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that the Eskenazi Museum actively acquires new a
 rtwork each year? These works serve to engage a range of audiences and fo
 ster research and learning.  Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, photographs\
 , and objects will be on view on the third floor in the Martha and David 
 Moore Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs Study and the William and Diane
  Itter Objects Study. Other newly acquired works can be explored in the g
 allery with the help of a self-guide.Drop in any time between 2 and 4 pm 
 to see the works and speak with curators who will be on hand to answer qu
 estions about the pieces they acquired for the collection.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Did you know
  that the Eskenazi Museum actively acquires new artwork each year? These 
 works serve to engage a range of audiences and foster research and learni
 ng.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, ph
 otographs\, and objects will be on view on the third floor in the Martha 
 and David Moore Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs Study and the William
  and Diane Itter Objects Study. Other newly acquired works can be explore
 d in the gallery with the help of a self-guide.</p><p style="font-weight:
  400\;"><strong>Drop in any time between 2 and 4 pm</strong> to see the w
 orks and speak with curators who will be on hand to answer questions abou
 t the pieces they acquired for the collection.</p>
